    {
        "name": "Babesiosis",
        "name_ja": "バベシア症",
        "symptoms": {"lethargy", "fever", "collapse", "weight_loss", "bloated_abdomen"},
        "description": "Tick-transmitted intraerythrocytic protozoan infection. Species in dogs: Babesia canis (Europe - Dermacentor reticulatus), B. gibsoni (Asia, Mediterranean - Haemaphysalis), B. vogeli (tropical/subtropical - Rhipicephalus sanguineus), B. conradae (Western USA), B. rossi (Africa - most virulent). In Japan: B. gibsoni is primary pathogen (Haemaphysalis longicornis tick vector; also dog-to-dog transmission via fighting, blood transfusion, transplacental). Breed predisposition: American Pit Bull Terriers, Staffordshire Bull Terriers (for B. gibsoni - fighting bite transmission). Clinical spectrum: subclinical carrier to severe hemolytic crisis, multi-organ failure. Classic presentation: acute-onset hemolytic anemia, fever, splenomegaly, hemoglobinuria (dark urine). Complications: IMHA-like picture, DIC, acute kidney injury, SIRS.",
        "description_ja": "マダニ媒介性の赤血球内原虫感染症。犬の原因種：Babesia canis（ヨーロッパ--Dermacentorマダニ）、B. gibsoni（アジア・地中海--Haemaphysalisマダニ）、B. vogeli（熱帯/亜熱帯--Rhipicepalus）、B. conradae（米西部）、B. rossi（アフリカ--最も病原性強い）。日本：B. gibsoniが主病原（Haemaphysalis longicornisマダニ媒介；咬傷・輸血・胎盤経由での犬間伝播も）。好発品種：アメリカン・ピット・ブル・テリア・スタッフォードシャー・ブル・テリア（B. gibsoni--咬傷伝播）。臨床スペクトラム：無症状キャリアから重篤な溶血性クリシス・多臓器不全まで。典型的発症：急性溶血性貧血・発熱・脾腫・ヘモグロビン尿（赤/褐色尿）。合併症：IMHA様・DIC・急性腎障害・SIRS。",
        "pathophysiology": "Babesia sporozoites injected via tick saliva during feeding (>24h attachment required for B. canis transmission; B. gibsoni may transmit faster via fighting bites). ERYTHROCYTIC CYCLE: merozoites invade RBCs → trophozoites divide by binary fission within RBC → form merozoite tetrads ('Maltese cross' or paired pyriform bodies) → RBC rupture releases new merozoites → reinfect new RBCs. HEMOLYSIS mechanisms: (1) Intravascular: direct RBC membrane disruption by parasite → hemoglobin release into plasma → hemoglobinemia + hemoglobinuria. (2) Extravascular: opsonization of parasitized RBCs with parasite antigens + host immunoglobulins → macrophage phagocytosis in spleen/liver. (3) IMMUNE-MEDIATED COMPONENT: B. gibsoni infection triggers anti-RBC antibodies (positive Coombs test in 50-80% of cases) - genuine IMHA superimposed on parasitic infection - explains treatment refractoriness to antiparasitic drugs alone. SPLENOMEGALY: spleen is primary site of erythrophagocytosis + extramedullary erythropoiesis. SEVERE DISEASE: parasitemia-induced cytokine storm (TNF-alpha, IL-1, IL-6) → vascular endothelial injury → SIRS → DIC → multiorgan failure. Cerebral babesiosis (B. rossi/canis): RBC sequestration in brain microvessels → cerebral hypoxia → seizures, coma.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "マダニ吸血中にバベシアスポロゾイトが注入（B. canisの伝播には>24時間の吸着が必要；B. gibsoniは咬傷でより速く伝播）。赤血球内サイクル：メロゾイトが赤血球に侵入→栄養体が赤血球内で二分裂→メロゾイト四分体（マルタ十字または対状梨形体）形成→赤血球破裂→新たなメロゾイトが放出され新赤血球に再感染。溶血の機序：(1)血管内：寄生虫による赤血球膜の直接破壊→ヘモグロビン遊離→ヘモグロビン血症＋ヘモグロビン尿症；(2)血管外：寄生虫抗原＋宿主免疫グロブリンによる感染赤血球のオプソニン化→脾臓/肝臓でのマクロファージ食作用；(3)免疫介在性成分：B. gibsoni感染で抗赤血球抗体誘導（症例の50〜80%でクームス試験陽性）--寄生虫感染に重なった真のIMHA--抗寄生虫薬単独での治療難治性の説明。脾腫：脾臓が赤血球食作用と髄外造血の主要部位。重症疾患：サイトカインストーム（TNF-alpha・IL-1・IL-6）→血管内皮傷害→SIRS→DIC→多臓器不全。脳バベシア症（B. rossi/canis）：脳微小血管での赤血球鬱滞→大脳低酸素→発作・昏睡。",
        "causes": "Babesia spp. (protozoan parasite) transmitted by Ixodid ticks. B. gibsoni in Japan via Haemaphysalis longicornis and dog bites (pit bull-type breeds). B. vogeli worldwide via Rhipicephalus sanguineus (brown dog tick). Direct transmission: dog fighting bites (B. gibsoni), blood transfusion, transplacental (documented in B. gibsoni).",
        "causes_ja": "バベシア原虫（マダニ媒介）。日本ではB. gibsoniがHaemaphysalis longicornisマダニと犬の咬傷（ピット・ブル型品種）で伝播。B. vogeliは世界的にRhipicephalus sanguineus（コイタマダニ）で媒介。直接伝播：闘犬での咬傷（B. gibsoni）・輸血・胎盤経由（B. gibsoniで記録あり）。",
        "treatment": "B. gibsoni (Japan) - MOST IMPORTANT: (1) Atovaquone 13.3 mg/kg PO q8h WITH FOOD (fat enhances absorption; drug of choice for B. gibsoni - inhibits parasite cytochrome bc1 complex) + azithromycin 10 mg/kg PO q24h x 10 days (synergistic). This combination achieves PCR negativity in ~50-70% of cases (recurrence common - monthly PCR monitoring recommended). (2) Alternative (if atovaquone unavailable/expensive): imidocarb dipropionate 5.0-6.6 mg/kg IM or SC, repeat in 14 days (more effective for B. canis/vogeli than B. gibsoni; pretreat with atropine 0.05 mg/kg SC to prevent cholinergic side effects). (3) Clindamycin 12.5 mg/kg PO q12h x 7-10 days (adjunctive for B. gibsoni). B. canis (Europe): imidocarb dipropionate 6.6 mg/kg SC single dose often curative. SUPPORTIVE CARE (all species): (4) Blood transfusion: PCV <15% or acute hemolytic crisis - fresh whole blood or pRBCs 10-15 mL/kg; oxyglobin if available; aggressively resuscitate. (5) IV fluids: LRS for perfusion support - monitor for fluid overload (hemolytic anemia reduces O2 carrying capacity). (6) Immunosuppression (if IMHA component present - positive Coombs): prednisone 1-2 mg/kg/day after anti-parasitic started (do NOT use before anti-parasitic - may worsen parasitemia). (7) DIC management: fresh frozen plasma (FFP) 10-15 mL/kg if PT/aPTT prolonged; heparin 150-250 IU/kg SC q6-8h if DIC confirmed. (8) Doxycycline 10 mg/kg PO q24h for co-infection with Ehrlichia (tick-borne co-infection common). (9) Tick prevention: monthly isoxazoline (fluralaner, sarolaner) - critical for prevention and re-infection prevention.",
        "treatment_ja": "B. gibsoni（日本）--最重要：(1)アトバコン13.3 mg/kg PO q8h（食事と同時--脂肪が吸収促進；B. gibsoniの第一選択--寄生虫のシトクロムbc1複合体阻害）＋アジスロマイシン10 mg/kg PO q24h×10日（相乗効果）。この組み合わせで約50〜70%がPCR陰性化（再発多い--月1回のPCRモニタリング推奨）。(2)代替（アトバコン入手困難時）：イミドカルブ5.0〜6.6 mg/kg IMまたはSC、14日後に反復（B. canisに最も有効；コリン作動性副作用予防のためアトロピン0.05 mg/kg SC前投薬）。(3)クリンダマイシン12.5 mg/kg PO q12h×7〜10日（B. gibsoniへの補助療法）。B. canis（ヨーロッパ）：イミドカルブ6.6 mg/kg SC単回で治癒することが多い。支持療法：PCV<15%または急性溶血クリシスに輸血（新鮮全血または濃厚赤血球10〜15 mL/kg）；輸液（LRS）；IMHA成分（クームス陽性）にはプレドニゾロン1〜2 mg/kg/日（抗寄生虫薬開始後に投与）；DICにはFFP＋ヘパリン；エールリヒア重複感染にドキシサイクリン；月1回イソオキサゾリン系ノミマダニ駆除薬。",
        "prognosis": "B. canis with imidocarb: 90%+ clinical cure (but may remain PCR-positive - subclinical carrier). B. gibsoni with atovaquone/azithromycin: 50-70% PCR negativity (recurrence common; long-term carrier state). Severe disease (cerebral babesiosis, DIC, AKI): mortality 20-50% despite treatment. Post-treatment Coombs-positive dogs: relapse risk with stress/immunosuppression. Regular PCR monitoring (1, 3, 6 months post-treatment) recommended to detect relapse.",
        "prognosis_ja": "B. canis＋イミドカルブ：>90%の臨床的治癒（PCR陽性が持続するキャリア状態は残存）。B. gibsoni＋アトバコン/アジスロマイシン：50〜70%がPCR陰性化（再発多い；長期キャリア状態）。重症（脳バベシア・DIC・AKI）：治療にもかかわらず死亡率20〜50%。治療後クームス陽性犬：ストレス/免疫抑制で再発リスク。治療後1・3・6ヶ月のPCRモニタリング推奨。",
        "prevention": "Year-round tick prevention (monthly isoxazoline - fluralaner/sarolaner; topical permethrin for outdoor dogs). Avoid tick habitats. Screen blood donors by PCR. Prevent dog fighting. Spay/neuter to reduce roaming. Test breeding dogs (transplacental transmission).",
        "prevention_ja": "通年マダニ予防（月1回イソオキサゾリン系--フルラネル/サロラネル；屋外犬にはパーメトリン外用）。マダニ生息地への立ち入り回避。輸血ドナーのPCRスクリーニング。闘犬防止。去勢手術（徘徊防止）。繁殖犬の検査（胎盤経由伝播）。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "Blood smear examination (Giemsa stain): intraerythrocytic organisms - B. canis large (paired pyriform, up to 5 micron); B. gibsoni small (ring forms, 1-2.5 micron, resembles Theileria); sensitivity 50-80% in acute phase; negative smear does not exclude",
            "PCR (whole blood, EDTA): species-specific PCR - definitive species identification (critical for treatment selection: atovaquone for B. gibsoni, imidocarb for B. canis/vogeli); detect low parasitemia carriers; monitor treatment response; more sensitive than smear",
            "CBC: regenerative hemolytic anemia (low PCV/HCT, reticulocytosis, polychromasia, spherocytes, schistocytes); thrombocytopenia (>80% of cases); neutrophilia or neutropenia (severe cases)",
            "Coombs test (direct antiglobulin test): positive in 50-80% of B. gibsoni cases - confirms immune-mediated hemolytic component (requires combined antiparasitic + immunosuppressive treatment); negative does not exclude B. canis",
            "Chemistry + urinalysis: hemoglobinuria (pink/brown urine supernatant - distinguish from hematuria by centrifugation); bilirubinuria; AKI (elevated BUN/creatinine); hypoglycemia (severe cases); hepatic enzyme elevation",
            "Coagulation profile (PT, aPTT, D-dimer, fibrinogen): DIC assessment - common in severe babesiosis; thrombocytopenia already present from CBC; D-dimer elevation + prolonged PT/aPTT = DIC - poor prognosis",
        ],
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult"},
    },
