    {
        "name": "Pericardial Effusion",
        "name_ja": "心嚢水貯留",
        "symptoms": {"difficulty_breathing", "bloated_abdomen", "appetite_loss", "lethargy", "rapid_breathing"},
        "description": "Accumulation of fluid within the pericardial sac causing cardiac compression and hemodynamic compromise. Most common cause in dogs: cardiac tamponade from neoplastic effusion (hemangiosarcoma of right atrium/right auricle — 70% of cases in large breeds; heart base tumor/chemodectoma — 10-20%). Other causes: idiopathic pericardial effusion (benign, especially Golden Retriever, Labrador), pericarditis (infectious, immune-mediated), left atrial tear (MMVD), coagulopathy. CARDIAC TAMPONADE: when intrapericardial pressure exceeds right heart filling pressure → impaired venous return → reduced cardiac output → distributive/obstructive shock. URGENCY: pericardiocentesis is life-saving and diagnostic.",
        "description_ja": "心嚢内への体液貯留による心臓圧迫と血行動態障害。犬での最多原因：腫瘍性心嚢水（右心房/右心耳の血管肉腫——大型犬のケースの約70%；心基部腫瘍/化学受容器腫——10〜20%）。その他：特発性心嚢水（良性；ゴールデン・レトリーバー、ラブラドールに多い）・心外膜炎（感染性・免疫介在性）・左房裂傷（MMVD）・凝固障害。心タンポナーデ：心嚢内圧が右心充満圧を超えると静脈還流障害→心拍出量低下→分布性/閉塞性ショック。緊急性：心嚢穿刺が救命的かつ診断的処置。",
        "pathophysiology": "The pericardium is a fibrous, non-distensible sac. Small volumes of effusion can be tolerated acutely; however, rapid accumulation (even small volumes, e.g., 100-200 mL) causes steep pressure rise (pericardial compliance curve). Once intrapericardial pressure (IPP) equals or exceeds right ventricular diastolic pressure: right ventricular diastolic collapse (classic echo finding) → impaired right ventricular filling → reduced pulmonary blood flow → reduced left ventricular preload → reduced cardiac output → compensatory tachycardia, peripheral vasoconstriction. Classic tamponade physiology: PARADOXUS pulsus (systolic BP decrease >10 mmHg on inspiration) — because inspiratory right ventricular expansion compresses already-compressed left ventricle in non-distensible pericardium (ventricular interdependence). Central venous pressure (CVP) rises due to impaired venous return → jugular vein distension, ascites (from hepatic congestion). BECK triad: hypotension + muffled heart sounds + jugular venous distension. Hemangiosarcoma: predilection for right atrium/auricle; highly vascular, friable → hemorrhagic effusion (bloody, non-clotting); rapid tumor growth causes sudden rupture; prognosis poor.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "心嚢は非伸縮性の線維性嚢。急速な貯留（少量でも100〜200 mL）では心嚢コンプライアンス曲線が急峻に上昇し心嚢内圧（IPP）が急上昇。IPPが右室拡張期圧と同等以上になると：右室拡張期虚脱（心エコーの古典的所見）→右室充満障害→肺血流低下→左室前負荷低下→心拍出量低下→代償性頻脈と末梢血管収縮。古典的タンポナーデ生理：奇脈（吸気時収縮期BP低下>10 mmHg）——吸気時右室膨張が非伸縮性心嚢内で圧迫された左室をさらに圧迫（心室相互依存性）。中心静脈圧上昇→頸静脈怒張・腹水（肝うっ血）。Beckの三徴：低血圧＋心音減弱＋頸静脈怒張。血管肉腫：右心房/心耳への好発→高血管性・脆弱→血性・非凝固性滲出液；急速な腫瘍成長→突然破裂；予後不良。",
        "causes": "Neoplastic (hemangiosarcoma right atrium 70%, chemodectoma 10-20%), idiopathic (benign, especially Golden Retriever/Labrador), pericarditis (bacterial, fungal, immune-mediated), left atrial tear (severe MMVD), coagulopathy, trauma, uremia.",
        "causes_ja": "腫瘍性（右心房血管肉腫70%、化学受容器腫10〜20%）、特発性良性（ゴールデン・ラブラドールに多い）、心外膜炎（細菌性・真菌性・免疫介在性）、左房裂傷（重度MMVD）、凝固障害、外傷、尿毒症。",
        "treatment": "EMERGENCY PERICARDIOCENTESIS (tamponade): (1) Right parasternal approach (4th-6th ICS, 14-16G over-the-needle catheter with 3-way stopcock); ultrasound-guided is gold standard — identifies fluid location and avoids coronary vessels. Sedate with butorphanol 0.2 mg/kg IV ± midazolam 0.2 mg/kg IV (avoid acepromazine — causes hypotension). (2) Drain as much fluid as possible; fluid that clots = ventricular puncture (inadvertent); true pericardial effusion does not clot (no fibrinogen). (3) Send fluid for: cytology, culture, PE:TP ratio (>0.3 suggests exudate/neoplasm). (4) Monitor ECG during procedure — VPCs from pericardial irritation common, usually self-limiting. POST-PERICARDIOCENTESIS: expect hemodynamic improvement within minutes. DEFINITIVE MANAGEMENT: (5) Idiopathic pericardial effusion: pericardiectomy (subtotal vs. pericardial window) if recurrence ≥2 episodes or large tumor absent; second episode: recommend pericardiectomy. (6) Hemangiosarcoma: doxorubicin-based chemotherapy (doxorubicin 30 mg/m2 IV q21d; VAC protocol: vincristine + doxorubicin + cyclophosphamide); surgical resection of accessible right auricular masses at time of pericardiectomy; prognosis poor (median survival 1-2 months untreated, 4-6 months with chemo). (7) Chemodectoma: pericardiectomy only (slow growing, chemo not effective); median survival 18 months post-pericardiectomy.",
        "treatment_ja": "緊急心嚢穿刺（タンポナーデ）：(1)右傍胸骨アプローチ（第4〜6肋間腔、14〜16G静脈留置カテーテル＋三方コック）；超音波ガイド下が標準（体液位置確認・冠動脈回避）。鎮静：ブトルファノール0.2 mg/kg IV±ミダゾラム0.2 mg/kg IV（アセプロマジン禁忌——低血圧誘発）。(2)できる限り液体を排出；凝固する液体=心室穿刺（事故）；真の心嚢水は凝固しない（フィブリノーゲンなし）。(3)液体検査：細胞診・培養・PE:TP比（>0.3=滲出液/腫瘍示唆）。(4)処置中ECGモニタリング（VPCsは心嚢刺激から発生、通常自然消退）。定治療：(5)特発性心嚢水：再発2回以上または腫瘍なしで心嚢膜切除術（亜全摘または窓作成）。(6)血管肉腫：ドキソルビシン系化学療法（ドキソルビシン30 mg/m2 IV 21日毎）；アクセス可能な右心耳腫瘤は心嚢膜切除時に同時切除；予後不良（未治療で生存期間中央値1〜2ヶ月、化学療法で4〜6ヶ月）。(7)化学受容器腫：心嚢膜切除術のみ（緩徐成長、化学療法無効）；術後生存期間中央値18ヶ月。",
        "prognosis": "Idiopathic pericardial effusion: excellent after pericardiectomy (low recurrence, normal life expectancy). Hemangiosarcoma: poor (median survival 4-6 months with doxorubicin, 1-2 months without). Chemodectoma: good after pericardiectomy (median 18 months). Recurrence rates after single pericardiocentesis without pericardiectomy: 50-70% within 6 months.",
        "prognosis_ja": "特発性心嚢水：心嚢膜切除術後に予後優良（再発率低、正常な余命）。血管肉腫：予後不良（ドキソルビシン投与で中央値4〜6ヶ月、未治療で1〜2ヶ月）。化学受容器腫：心嚢膜切除術後に良好（中央値18ヶ月）。心嚢穿刺のみ（心嚢膜切除なし）での6ヶ月以内の再発率：50〜70%。",
        "prevention": "No specific prevention. Annual cardiac ultrasound screening in predisposed breeds (Golden Retriever, German Shepherd, Boxer) from age 5 onwards.",
        "prevention_ja": "確立された予防法なし。好発犬種（ゴールデン・レトリーバー、ジャーマン・シェパード、ボクサー）では5歳以降から年1回の心臓超音波スクリーニングを推奨。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "Echocardiography (urgent): confirms pericardial effusion; assesses right ventricular diastolic collapse (tamponade sign); identifies cardiac masses (right atrial mass = hemangiosarcoma until proven otherwise); guides pericardiocentesis needle entry",
            "ECG: sinus tachycardia (compensation); electrical alternans (alternating QRS amplitude — classic sign of large pericardial effusion compressing heart as it swings within fluid); low voltage QRS complexes (<1 mV in all leads)",
            "Chest radiographs: globoid (round, flask-shaped) cardiac silhouette — non-specific but raises suspicion; differentiate from dilated cardiomyopathy; pleural effusion may also be present",
            "Pericardial fluid cytology + culture: RBC-rich, non-clotting (hemorrhagic effusion); neoplastic cells in 20-30% of tumor-associated effusions; PE:TP > 0.3 = exudate/neoplasm; culture for infectious pericarditis",
            "CBC + chemistry panel: thrombocytopenia (coagulopathy risk in hemangiosarcoma), anemia from hemorrhagic effusion, ALT elevation (hepatic congestion from elevated CVP), BUN/creatinine baseline",
            "Abdominal ultrasound: screen for splenic hemangiosarcoma (most common primary site — right atrial HSA often metastatic); hepatic masses; concurrent abdominal effusion",
        ],
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult"},
    },
