            "CBC: neutrophilia (left shift), lymphopenia; chemistry: hypoalbuminemia, elevated globulins (chronic disease pattern); urinalysis: rule out concurrent UTI (Type II trigger)",
            "Tick-borne disease panel (4Dx or PCR): Borrelia burgdorferi, Ehrlichia, Anaplasma — essential rule-out before immunosuppression",
            "Radiographs of affected joints: non-erosive IMPA — joint effusion only, no bony erosions; erosive IMPA (rare) — subchondral bone lysis, periarticular sclerosis; rule out septic arthritis (gas in joint, bone destruction)",
