    {
        "name": "Urethral Obstruction",
        "name_ja": "尿道閉塞",
        "symptoms": {"straining_urinate", "blood_urine", "vomiting", "collapse", "lethargy"},
        "description": "Complete blockage of urine outflow causing uremia, electrolyte disturbances, and bladder rupture risk. Most common in male dogs (narrow urethra at os penis and ischial arch). Causes: urolithiasis (most common - struvite, CaOx, urate), urethral stricture, urethral mucous plug, prostatic neoplasia, blood clot, reflex dyssynergia. Cats more commonly affected than dogs. Signs: repeated squatting without urination, crying in pain, distended painful bladder, post-renal azotemia, bradycardia (hyperkalemia). Death from hyperkalemia-induced cardiac arrest or bladder rupture within 24-72h if untreated.",
        "description_ja": "尿排出の完全閉塞による尿毒症・電解質異常・膀胱破裂リスク。雄犬に最多（陰茎骨と坐骨弓での細い尿道）。原因：尿石症（最多--ストルバイト・CaOx・尿酸塩）・尿道狭窄・尿道粘液プラグ・前立腺腫瘍・血液凝塊・反射性排尿筋括約筋協調不全。犬より猫に多い。症状：尿を出さずに繰り返す排尿姿勢・痛みで鳴く・拡張した有痛性膀胱・後腎性窒素血症・徐脈（高カリウム血症）。未治療では高カリウム血症誘発の心停止または膀胱破裂で24〜72時間以内に死亡。",
        "pathophysiology": "Complete urethral obstruction prevents all urine from exiting the bladder. Pathophysiological cascade: (1) BLADDER OVERDISTENSION: urine production continues (kidneys maintain glomerular filtration until uremia develops) → progressive bladder distension → risk of detrusor muscle damage (acute overstretching → myogenic failure post-obstruction, bladder atony) → eventual bladder wall ischemia → potential bladder rupture (especially if trauma or pre-existing bladder wall disease). (2) POST-RENAL AZOTEMIA: urine back-pressure → decreased glomerular filtration rate → BUN/creatinine accumulation; hydroureter + hydronephrosis if prolonged (>24-48h). (3) HYPERKALEMIA: inability to excrete potassium in urine → potassium accumulates in blood; uremia also shifts K+ out of cells (decreased Na-K-ATPase activity); hyperkalemia at >6.5 mEq/L: ECG changes (tall peaked T waves, prolonged PR interval, wide QRS) → ventricular arrhythmias → cardiac arrest risk; >8.0 mEq/L: severe bradycardia, sine wave pattern, cardiac standstill. (4) METABOLIC ACIDOSIS: decreased H+ excretion → accumulating acid; worsens hyperkalemia (H+/K+ antiport shifts K+ out of cells); respiratory compensation (Kussmaul breathing). (5) UREMIA: accumulation of uremic toxins (urea, creatinine, organic acids, middle molecules) → uremic gastroenteritis (vomiting, anorexia), uremic encephalopathy, platelet dysfunction (uremic platelet inhibition), pericarditis. (6) DILUTIONAL HYPONATREMIA: develops when uremia causes inappropriate water retention; paradoxical - cannot excrete free water. Bladder wall ischemia and post-decompression diuresis (post-obstructive diuresis = massive urine production after relief) require vigilant fluid therapy.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "完全尿道閉塞により全ての尿が膀胱から排出できなくなる。病態カスケード：(1)膀胱過拡張：尿産生は継続（腎臓は尿毒症が発症するまで糸球体濾過を維持）→膀胱の進行性拡張→排尿筋損傷リスク（急性過伸展→閉塞後筋原性不全・膀胱無力症）→膀胱壁虚血→膀胱破裂リスク。(2)後腎性窒素血症：尿の逆圧→GFR低下→BUN/クレアチニン蓄積；遷延する場合は尿管拡張＋水腎症。(3)高カリウム血症：カリウムを尿中排泄できない→血中カリウム蓄積；尿毒症もNa-K-ATPase活性低下により細胞外へのK+シフトを起こす；>6.5 mEq/L：ECG変化（tall peaked T波・PR間隔延長・QRS拡幅）→心室性不整脈→心停止リスク；>8.0 mEq/L：重篤な徐脈・サイン波パターン・心停止。(4)代謝性アシドーシス：H+排泄低下→酸蓄積；高カリウム血症を悪化させる（H+/K+対向輸送でK+が細胞外に移動）。(5)尿毒症：尿毒素蓄積→尿毒症性胃腸炎・尿毒症性脳症・血小板機能異常・心膜炎。(6)希釈性低ナトリウム血症：尿毒症による不適切な水分貯留。膀胱壁虚血と閉塞解除後の利尿（閉塞後利尿=解除後の大量尿産生）には細心の輸液管理が必要。",
        "causes": "Urolithiasis (struvite - infection-induced; CaOx - idiopathic hypercalciuria; urate - portosystemic shunt, Dalmatian breed), urethral stricture (post-inflammatory or traumatic), prostatic disease (hyperplasia, neoplasia), blood clot (bladder/urethral hemorrhage), urethral neoplasia (transitional cell carcinoma), reflex dyssynergia (neurological - dyscoordination of sphincter during voiding).",
        "causes_ja": "尿石症（ストルバイト--感染誘発性；CaOx--特発性高カルシウム尿症；尿酸塩--PSS・ダルメシアン品種）・尿道狭窄（炎症後または外傷性）・前立腺疾患（過形成・腫瘍）・血液凝塊（膀胱/尿道出血）・尿道腫瘍（移行上皮癌）・反射性排尿筋括約筋協調不全（神経学的）。",
        "treatment": "EMERGENCY STABILIZATION: (1) IV catheter (cephalic vein) - avoid jugular if bladder rupture possible (coagulopathy). (2) ECG IMMEDIATELY: assess hyperkalemia effects; if bradycardia + ECG changes (peaked T, wide QRS), treat hyperkalemia before catheterization: calcium gluconate 10% 0.5-1.0 mL/kg IV slow (cardiac membrane stabilizer - does NOT lower K+ but protects heart); sodium bicarbonate 1-2 mEq/kg IV slow (shifts K+ into cells); 50% dextrose 0.5 mL/kg IV + regular insulin 0.25-0.5 IU/kg IV (K+ shifts intracellularly). (3) IV fluids: 0.9% NaCl (normal saline - NO potassium-containing fluids like LRS/Plasmalyte until K+ controlled); 20-30 mL/kg bolus; corrects dehydration, dilutes K+, improves renal perfusion. RELIEVE OBSTRUCTION: (4) Urethral catheterization: lubricate well; retropulsion with saline flush (push stone back to bladder); 3.5-5 Fr polypropylene catheter; collect urine for culture/sediment. (5) If catheterization fails: cystocentesis (needle aspiration of bladder) to decompress and stabilize before reattempting. (6) Perineal urethrostomy (PU): if urethral stricture or recurrent obstruction at os penis - permanent diversion. DEFINITIVE (STONE REMOVAL): (7) Medical dissolution (struvite only): calculolytic diet (Royal Canin Urinary S/O, Hill s s/d) + antibiotics for infection; 4-12 weeks dissolution. (8) Surgical urethrotomy or cystotomy: CaOx stones (not dissolvable). (9) Laser lithotripsy: non-invasive for stones at urethra. POST-DECOMPRESSION: (10) Post-obstructive diuresis monitoring: urine output may be 2-10x normal; match fluid intake to output (0.9% NaCl); prevent hypokalemia and hyponatremia; continuous electrolyte monitoring.",
        "treatment_ja": "緊急安定化：(1)IV留置針（頭静脈）。(2)即時ECG：高カリウム血症の影響を評価；徐脈＋ECG変化（tall T波・wide QRS）があればカテーテル挿入前に高カリウム血症を治療：グルコン酸カルシウム10% 0.5〜1.0 mL/kg IV（心膜安定化--K+は下がらないが心臓を保護）；炭酸水素ナトリウム1〜2 mEq/kg IV（K+を細胞内にシフト）；50%ブドウ糖0.5 mL/kg IV＋レギュラーインスリン0.25〜0.5 IU/kg IV。(3)輸液：0.9%食塩水（通常食塩水--K+含有液（LRS/Plasmalyte）はK+制御まで禁止）；20〜30 mL/kgボーラス。閉塞解除：(4)尿道カテーテル挿入：十分な潤滑；生食押し戻し（石を膀胱に戻す）；3.5〜5 Frポリプロピレンカテーテル；培養/沈渣のために尿を採取。(5)カテーテル挿入が不可能な場合：膀胱穿刺（減圧のために針吸引）。(6)会陰部尿道造口術（PU）：尿道狭窄または陰茎骨での再発閉塞時。確定的（結石除去）：(7)内科的溶解（ストルバイトのみ）：計算食＋感染への抗菌薬；4〜12週の溶解。(8)外科的尿道切開または膀胱切開：CaOx（溶解不可）。(9)レーザー砕石術。閉塞解除後：(10)閉塞後利尿モニタリング：尿産生量が正常の2〜10倍になる可能性；尿産生量に合わせた輸液（0.9%食塩水）；低カリウム血症・低ナトリウム血症の予防。",
        "prognosis": "Uncomplicated obstruction <24h: excellent (95%+ resolution). Obstruction >48-72h with uremia/hyperkalemia: good if aggressive treatment initiated promptly; renal function recovers in most cases. Bladder rupture: guarded (uroabdomen requires surgery + peritoneal lavage; 50-75% survival). Recurrence rate: struvite 10-25% with dietary management; CaOx 50-75% without dietary intervention. Urethral TCC: poor (infiltrative neoplasia - palliative only).",
        "prognosis_ja": "単純な閉塞<24時間：優秀（>95%解決）。閉塞>48〜72時間＋尿毒症/高カリウム血症：迅速な積極的治療で良好；多くの症例で腎機能回復。膀胱破裂：慎重（尿腹膜炎は手術＋腹膜洗浄が必要；生存率50〜75%）。再発率：食事管理でのストルバイト10〜25%；食事介入なしのCaOx 50〜75%。尿道TCC：不良（浸潤性腫瘍--緩和のみ）。",
        "prevention": "Dietary management based on stone type (commercial calculolytic diets). Increased water intake (canned food, water fountains). Urine pH monitoring. Treat concurrent UTI. Monitor dogs with known predispositions (Dalmatian, Bulldog) with periodic urinalysis.",
        "prevention_ja": "結石型に基づいた食事管理（市販の計算食）。水分摂取量の増加（缶詰食・給水器）。尿pH監視。同時UTIの治療。既知の素因を持つ犬（ダルメシアン・ブルドッグ）での定期尿検査。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "ECG (immediate): hyperkalemia-induced changes (peaked T waves, prolonged PR interval, widened QRS complex, sine wave, bradycardia); >6.5 mEq/L = cardiac effects; continuous monitoring during treatment; atrial standstill = severe (>8.0 mEq/L)",
            "Chemistry panel (stat): BUN/creatinine (post-renal azotemia severity); potassium (hyperkalemia - life-threatening); CO2/bicarbonate (metabolic acidosis); phosphorus (rises with uremia); glucose; total protein",
            "Abdominal radiographs (2-view): radiopaque stones (struvite, CaOx visible; urate radiolucent); stone location (urethra vs bladder vs ureter); bladder distension; free peritoneal fluid (bladder rupture)",
            "Urinalysis + urine culture/sensitivity: crystalluria (struvite = coffin-lid crystals; CaOx = calcium oxalate monohydrate dumbbell or dihydrate envelope; urate = thorn-apple); bacteriuria/pyuria (infection); pH (struvite >7.0; CaOx <7.0)",
            "Abdominal ultrasound: bladder size and wall integrity; stone echogenicity and acoustic shadowing; hydroureter (bilateral obstruction or prolonged); prostatic assessment (mass, abscess); uroabdomen (free fluid around bladder)",
            "Stone mineral analysis (post-retrieval): definitive composition (infrared spectroscopy or crystallography); determines dissolution protocol eligibility (struvite = medical; CaOx = surgical mandatory); guides dietary prevention",
        ],
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult"},
    },
