    {
        "name": "Immune-Mediated Polyarthritis",
        "name_ja": "免疫介在性多発性関節炎",
        "symptoms": {"stiffness", "swollen_joints", "fever", "lethargy", "reluctance_move"},
        "description": "Non-infectious inflammatory joint disease affecting multiple joints due to immune complex deposition and autoimmune attack. Classified as: (1) Type I (idiopathic - no identifiable cause, 50% of cases); (2) Type II (reactive, secondary to distant infection - UTI, endocarditis, pneumonia); (3) Type III (secondary to gastrointestinal disease - IBD, hepatitis); (4) Type IV (secondary to neoplasia - paraneoplastic). Breed predisposition: Akita, Shar Pei, Beagle, Weimaraner, Spaniel breeds (Type I). Dogs typically present with fever of unknown origin + shifting-leg lameness + joint effusion affecting 4+ joints. Differentiate from septic arthritis (requires joint culture) and rheumatoid arthritis (erosive, Type II IMPA - rarer).",
        "description_ja": "免疫複合体沈着と自己免疫性攻撃による複数関節の非感染性炎症性関節疾患。分類：(1)I型（特発性--同定可能な原因なし、症例の50%）；(2)II型（反応性、遠隔感染に続発--UTI・心内膜炎・肺炎）；(3)III型（消化管疾患に続発--IBD・肝炎）；(4)IV型（腫瘍に続発--腫瘍随伴性）。好発品種：秋田犬・シャー・ペイ・ビーグル・ワイマラナー・スパニエル品種（I型）。典型的発症：不明熱＋移動性跛行＋4つ以上の関節の関節液貯留。化膿性関節炎（関節液培養が必要）とリウマチ様関節炎（びらん性、II型IMPA--稀）との鑑別が重要。",
        "pathophysiology": "IMPA results from aberrant immune responses targeting synovial tissue. PATHOLOGICAL MECHANISMS: (1) IMMUNE COMPLEX DEPOSITION (primary mechanism in reactive forms): circulating antigen-antibody complexes deposit in synovial membrane and microvessels → complement activation → C3a/C5a-mediated neutrophil chemotaxis → neutrophil infiltration into joint space → release of proteolytic enzymes (elastase, collagenase, MMP-1/3/13) → synovial membrane destruction, cartilage degradation. (2) AUTOREACTIVE T CELL ATTACK (primary in idiopathic): aberrant CD4+ T helper cells recognize synovial antigens → Th1/Th17 polarization → TNF-alpha + IL-1beta + IL-6 + IL-17 production → synovitis, pannus formation. (3) TYPE III HYPERSENSITIVITY (serum sickness type): IgG or IgM antibody + antigen → soluble immune complex → deposits in synovium → Fc receptor activation on macrophages → inflammatory cascade. JOINT PATHOLOGY: synovial hypertrophy, villous proliferation, vascular pannus extension over cartilage, early cartilage proteoglycan loss. Non-erosive (most IMPA): pannus does not destroy underlying bone/cartilage = joint architecture preserved = reversible with treatment. Erosive IMPA (rare, rheumatoid-like): pannus invades and destroys bone/cartilage → periarticular erosions on radiographs → permanent joint damage. SYSTEMIC MANIFESTATIONS: immune complex deposition in other organs → glomerulonephritis (protein-losing nephropathy), uveitis, skin vasculitis; high-grade fever from IL-1/IL-6/TNF-alpha pyrogenic effect.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "IMPAは滑膜組織を標的とする異常免疫反応から生じる。病態機序：(1)免疫複合体沈着（反応性形態の主要機序）：循環する抗原抗体複合体が滑膜と微小血管に沈着→補体活性化→C3a/C5a介在性好中球走化性→関節腔への好中球浸潤→タンパク分解酵素（エラスターゼ・コラゲナーゼ・MMP-1/3/13）放出→滑膜破壊・軟骨変性。(2)自己反応性T細胞攻撃（特発性形態の主要）：異常なCD4+Tヘルパー細胞が滑膜抗原を認識→Th1/Th17偏極→TNF-alpha＋IL-1beta＋IL-6＋IL-17産生→滑膜炎・パンヌス形成。(3)III型過敏症（血清病型）：IgGまたはIgM抗体＋抗原→可溶性免疫複合体→滑膜に沈着→マクロファージのFc受容体活性化→炎症カスケード。関節病理：非びらん性（ほとんどのIMPA）：パンヌスは基礎骨/軟骨を破壊しない=関節構造保存=治療で可逆的。びらん性IMPA（稀、リウマチ様）：パンヌスが骨/軟骨に浸潤・破壊→X線上の関節周囲びらん→永久的関節損傷。全身症状：他臓器への免疫複合体沈着→糸球体腎炎・ブドウ膜炎・皮膚血管炎；IL-1/IL-6/TNF-alphaの発熱誘発作用による高体温。",
        "causes": "Primary (idiopathic, Type I): most common, no identifiable cause, breed predisposition. Secondary: Type II - concurrent infection (UTI, skin infection, endocarditis, prostatitis, pneumonia); Type III - GI disease (IBD, protein-losing enteropathy); Type IV - neoplasia (lymphoma, thymoma, carcinoma). Drug-induced (sulfonamides, cephalosporins, penicillin, vaccines).",
        "causes_ja": "原発性（特発性、I型）：最多、同定可能な原因なし、品種素因。続発性：II型--並存感染症（UTI・皮膚感染・心内膜炎・前立腺炎・肺炎）；III型--消化管疾患（IBD・タンパク喪失性腸疾患）；IV型--腫瘍（リンパ腫・胸腺腫・癌腫）。薬剤性（サルファ薬・セファロスポリン・ペニシリン・ワクチン）。",
        "treatment": "IDENTIFY AND TREAT SECONDARY CAUSES FIRST (critical): (1) Complete infectious/systemic workup before immunosuppression. (2) If secondary cause identified: treat primary cause (antibiotics for UTI, endoscopy/treatment for IBD) - IMPA may resolve without immunosuppression. PRIMARY IMMUNOSUPPRESSION: (3) Prednisolone 2-4 mg/kg/day PO (induction): most effective for idiopathic IMPA; rapid response (joint effusion resolves within 1-2 weeks, fever resolves 24-48h); titrate down over 3-6 months based on joint cytology improvement; long-term maintenance 0.5 mg/kg EOD. (4) Add azathioprine 2 mg/kg/day PO if: inadequate response to prednisone alone, intolerable prednisone side effects, or erosive IMPA; onset 4-6 weeks; monitor CBC/chemistry q2-4 weeks (myelosuppression, hepatotoxicity). (5) Leflunomide 3-4 mg/kg/day PO: effective alternative for IMPA; inhibits pyrimidine synthesis (anti-proliferative for T and B cells); useful as prednisone-sparing agent in refractory cases. (6) Cyclosporine 5-10 mg/kg/day PO: calcineurin inhibitor; useful in concurrent skin/GI IMPA. (7) Mycophenolate mofetil 10-20 mg/kg/day PO: increasingly used for refractory cases. JOINT MANAGEMENT: (8) Rest during acute phase (2-3 weeks); gradual exercise resumption. (9) NSAIDs (after ruling out immunosuppression adequacy - NOT combined with steroids): meloxicam 0.1 mg/kg/day PO only if weaning steroids. MONITORING: (10) Joint cytology at 3-4 weeks (target: <5000 cells/microL, non-degenerate neutrophils); repeat as needed for taper decisions.",
        "treatment_ja": "続発性原因を最初に同定・治療（重要）：(1)免疫抑制前に完全な感染/全身スクリーニング。(2)続発性原因が同定された場合：基礎疾患を治療（UTIへの抗菌薬・IBDへの内視鏡/治療）--免疫抑制なしでIMPAが消退する可能性。免疫抑制療法：(3)プレドニゾロン2〜4 mg/kg/日PO（導入）：特発性IMPAに最有効；急速反応（関節液は1〜2週で消退、発熱は24〜48時間で消退）；3〜6ヶ月かけてテーパー；維持0.5 mg/kg EOD。(4)アザチオプリン2 mg/kg/日PO（プレドニゾロン単独で不十分な場合/副作用が許容できない場合/びらん性IMPA）：効果発現4〜6週；骨髄抑制・肝毒性モニタリング。(5)レフルノミド3〜4 mg/kg/日PO：有効な代替薬；ピリミジン合成阻害（T・B細胞抗増殖）。(6)シクロスポリン5〜10 mg/kg/日PO。(7)ミコフェノール酸モフェチル10〜20 mg/kg/日PO（難治例）。急性期は安静（2〜3週）；徐々に運動再開。モニタリング：3〜4週時に関節液細胞診（目標：<5000細胞/μL、非変性好中球）。",
        "prognosis": "Non-erosive idiopathic IMPA: good (70-80% achieve long-term remission with appropriate immunosuppression; relapse common when steroids stopped). Type II (secondary to infection): excellent if primary infection resolved. Type III/IV: depends on underlying disease management. Erosive IMPA: guarded (permanent joint damage; remission possible but deformity may persist). Recurrence: common (30-50%), especially when steroids tapered too rapidly.",
        "prognosis_ja": "非びらん性特発性IMPA：良好（70〜80%が適切な免疫抑制で長期寛解；ステロイド中止時に再発が多い）。II型（感染に続発）：基礎感染が解決すれば優秀。III/IV型：基礎疾患管理に依存。びらん性IMPA：慎重（永久的関節損傷；寛解は可能だが変形が残る可能性）。再発：一般的（30〜50%）、特にステロイドが急速にテーパーされた場合。",
        "prevention": "No established prevention. Early treatment of concurrent infections to prevent reactive IMPA. Avoid implicated drugs (sulfonamides) in predisposed breeds. Monitor ANA/RF titers in Akita/Shar Pei for early detection.",
        "prevention_ja": "確立された予防法なし。反応性IMPAを防ぐための同時感染症の早期治療。好発犬種での関与薬（サルファ薬）の回避。秋田犬/シャー・ペイでのANA/RF価のモニタリングによる早期発見。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "Joint fluid analysis (arthrocentesis - multiple joints): increased NCC (>3000 cells/microL, predominantly non-degenerate neutrophils 80-90% = inflammatory, non-septic); increased protein; negative culture (septic arthritis excluded); low viscosity; volume 0.2-1.0 mL per joint; target 3+ joints for diagnosis",
            "ANA (antinuclear antibody) + LE cell prep: positive in SLE-associated IMPA (Type I overlap); Akita breed: high ANA prevalence; also test RF (rheumatoid factor) for erosive IMPA; ANA >1:20 on IFA = significant",
            "Radiographs of multiple joints: non-erosive IMPA = soft tissue swelling, joint effusion (no periarticular erosions); erosive IMPA = periarticular erosions, narrowed joint spaces, bone remodeling; helps stage and classify IMPA",
            "Complete infectious/systemic workup: CBC (neutrophilia), chemistry (acute phase proteins - CRP, globulin), UA + culture (UTI as Type II trigger); chest radiographs (pulmonary neoplasia, pneumonia); abdominal ultrasound (neoplasia, lymphadenopathy)",
            "Tick-borne disease serology/PCR: Borrelia burgdorferi C6 ELISA, Ehrlichia canis, Anaplasma phagocytophilum, Rickettsia - all can cause reactive IMPA; important before starting immunosuppression",
            "Serum protein electrophoresis + complement levels (C3, C4): immune complex-mediated disease causes hyper-gammaglobulinemia (polyclonal); complement consumption (low C3/C4) in active immune complex disease; UPC ratio for glomerulonephritis from systemic immune complex deposition",
        ],
        "urgency": "high",
        "onset_pattern": {"subacute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult"},
    },
