    {
        "name": "Lagenidiosis",
        "name_ja": "ラゲニジウム症",
        "symptoms": {"skin_lesions", "lumps", "swelling", "limping_rl", "limping_rr"},
        "description": "Oomycete infection causing progressive cutaneous and subcutaneous granulomatous lesions, often in limbs.",
        "description_ja": "卵菌感染症で、四肢を中心に進行性の皮膚・皮下肉芽腫病変を起こす。",
        "pathophysiology": "Lagenidium giganteum forma caninum (and rare cases of L. karlingii) is a water-borne oomycete (Stramenopila kingdom, NOT a true fungus despite filamentous appearance) closely related to Pythium insidiosum. Distinguished from fungi by cell wall composition (cellulose and beta-glucans without ergosterol or chitin) and motile flagellated zoospores - this absence of ergosterol explains intrinsic resistance to azoles, polyenes, and other ergosterol-targeting antifungals. Infection acquired from warm freshwater environments (ponds, swamps, lakes - particularly southern US Gulf Coast states) when zoospores chemotactically migrate to and penetrate damaged skin or rarely intact mucosa. Hyphae invade subcutis, fascia, blood vessels, and lymphatics producing pyogranulomatous-eosinophilic inflammation with characteristic broad ribbon-like sparsely septate hyphae visible on histopathology. Disease pattern in dogs typically features (1) rapidly progressive ulcerative or proliferative cutaneous lesions on extremities, ventrum, or perineum; (2) regional lymphadenopathy with massive lymph node enlargement; (3) systemic dissemination in 50-70 percent of cases involving great vessels (aorta, vena cava with risk of fatal hemorrhage), thorax, abdomen, kidneys. Distinguished from cutaneous pythiosis (Pythium insidiosum) - which has GI/cutaneous predilection - by deeper invasion, more aggressive vascular involvement, and predominant peripheral lymph node involvement. Mean age at presentation 2-4 years; large breeds (Labradors, Pit Bulls) overrepresented in outdoor working/hunting scenarios.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "Lagenidium giganteum forma caninum（稀にL. karlingii）は水生卵菌（ストラメノパイル界、糸状外観だが真菌ではない）でPythium insidiosumに近縁。細胞壁組成（エルゴステロールやキチンなしのセルロース＋βグルカン）と運動性鞭毛遊走子により真菌と区別—エルゴステロール欠如によりアゾール、ポリエン、その他のエルゴステロール標的抗真菌薬に内因性耐性。温かい淡水環境（池、湿地、湖、特に米国南部メキシコ湾岸諸州）から感染獲得、遊走子が損傷皮膚または稀に無傷粘膜に走化性遊走し侵入。菌糸が皮下組織、筋膜、血管、リンパ管に侵入し化膿肉芽腫-好酸球性炎症を起こし、病理組織で特徴的な幅広いリボン状疎性隔壁菌糸を確認。犬の典型的疾患パターン：(1)四肢、腹側、会陰部の急速進行性潰瘍性または増殖性皮膚病変、(2)大規模リンパ節腫大を伴う限局性リンパ節腫脹、(3)50-70%の症例で大血管（大動脈、大静脈—致死的出血リスク）、胸腔、腹腔、腎を侵す全身播種。皮膚ピシウム症（Pythium insidiosum—消化管/皮膚好発）と区別される点：より深部侵襲、より積極的血管関与、優勢な末梢リンパ節関与。発症平均年齢2-4歳、大型犬種（ラブラドール、ピットブル）が屋外使役/狩猟シナリオで過剰代表。",
        "causes": "Exposure to warm freshwater (ponds, swamps, lakes) containing Lagenidium spp. zoospores. Geographic distribution endemic in southern US Gulf Coast (Florida, Louisiana, Texas, Mississippi) and tropical/subtropical regions worldwide. Risk factors: hunting/working dogs with frequent water exposure, breaches in skin barrier, swimming in standing water during warm months.",
        "causes_ja": "Lagenidium属遊走子を含む温かい淡水（池、湿地、湖）への曝露。地理的分布：米国南部メキシコ湾岸（フロリダ、ルイジアナ、テキサス、ミシシッピ）と熱帯・亜熱帯地域に流行。リスク因子：水曝露頻繁な狩猟・使役犬、皮膚バリア破綻、温暖期の止水域水泳。",
        "treatment": "Aggressive surgical resection with wide margins is the cornerstone of treatment - incomplete resection or topical/medical-only management nearly always fails. Diagnostic workup: cytology of FNA (broad ribbon-like hyphae), tissue biopsy with histopathology and PCR (genus-specific PCR distinguishes Lagenidium from Pythium - critical because treatment differs subtly), Lagenidium-specific ELISA serology where available. Imaging staging: thoracic radiographs, abdominal ultrasound, CT for vascular involvement (mandatory if great vessel suspected) - rule out aortic/vena caval invasion before surgery. Wide surgical excision: 3-5 cm margins minimum; limb amputation often necessary for distal lesions, en-bloc resection of regional lymph nodes. If incomplete excision (vascular involvement, non-resectable site), prognosis grave. Adjuvant medical therapy mandatory regardless of surgical completeness: itraconazole 10 mg/kg PO BID + terbinafine 10-15 mg/kg PO BID for 3-6 months minimum (combination superior to either alone despite intrinsic resistance, exhibits some synergy). Mefenoxam (oomyceticide veterinary used in plant agriculture, off-label experimental use) shows in vitro promise but no validated dosing for dogs. Prednisone 1-2 mg/kg PO SID may reduce eosinophilic inflammation and immune-mediated tissue damage adjunctively. Monitor monthly with imaging and serology titer; declining titer correlates with treatment success. Treatment for life if disseminated. Aggressive supportive care for great vessel rupture (rare survivors). Owner education on prognosis - recurrence rate high (50-70 percent) even after apparent surgical cure.",
        "treatment_ja": "広範マージンでの積極的外科切除が治療の中核—不完全切除または外用・内科のみの管理はほぼ常に失敗。診断検査：FNAの細胞診（幅広いリボン状菌糸）、組織生検と病理組織、PCR（属特異的PCRはLagenidiumとPythiumを区別—治療がやや異なるため重要）、利用可能ならLagenidium特異的ELISA血清抗体。画像病期分類：胸部X線、腹部超音波、CTで血管関与評価（大血管疑いあれば必須）—術前に大動脈/大静脈侵襲除外。広範外科切除：最低3-5 cmマージン、遠位病変では四肢切断要する場合多い、限局性リンパ節のen bloc切除。不完全切除（血管関与、非切除部位）では予後極めて不良。外科の完遂度に関わらず補助内科療法必須：イトラコナゾール10 mg/kg PO BID＋テルビナフィン10-15 mg/kg PO BIDを最低3-6ヶ月（内因性耐性ありでも併用が単剤より優れ、ある程度の相乗作用）。メフェノキサム（植物農業の卵菌駆除剤、適応外実験的使用）が試験管内で有望だが犬の有効投与量未確立。プレドニゾン1-2 mg/kg PO SIDが好酸球性炎症と免疫介在性組織損傷を補助的に軽減しうる。月1回の画像と血清抗体価で経過観察、抗体価低下は治療成功と相関。播種例は生涯治療。大血管破裂は積極的支持療法（生存稀）。予後について飼い主教育—外科的見かけ上治癒後でも再発率高い（50-70%）。",
        "prognosis": "Grave despite aggressive treatment. Survival rates: localized cutaneous-only with complete excision and combination therapy 30-50 percent at 1 year; disseminated disease <10 percent at 1 year. Most dogs die or are euthanized within 3-12 months from progression, recurrence, or vascular rupture. Surgical cure with negative margins and complete medical course offers best chance; rapid recurrence despite treatment indicates incomplete resection or undetected dissemination.",
        "prognosis_ja": "積極的治療しても極めて不良。生存率：完全切除と併用療法での皮膚限局のみで1年30-50%、播種例で1年<10%。多くの犬は進行、再発、血管破裂で3-12ヶ月以内に死亡または安楽死。マージン陰性の外科的治癒と完全内科コースで最良のチャンス、治療しても急速再発は不完全切除または未検出播種を示唆。",
        "prevention": "Avoid stagnant warm freshwater exposure in endemic regions during peak season (spring through fall). Limit hunting/working dog access to ponds and swamps. Promptly treat any skin breaches. No vaccine available. Education of owners in endemic areas about early signs - rapidly enlarging cutaneous lesion in extremity in working/hunting dog warrants prompt evaluation.",
        "prevention_ja": "流行地域でのピーク期（春-秋）の止水温暖淡水曝露回避。狩猟・使役犬の池・湿地アクセス制限。皮膚破綻の迅速治療。ワクチンなし。流行地域の飼い主への早期徴候教育—使役・狩猟犬の四肢の急速増大皮膚病変は迅速評価要。",
        "recommended_tests": [
            "FNA細胞診（幅広いリボン状菌糸） (FNA cytology - broad ribbon-like hyphae)",
            "病理組織検査とGMS染色 (Histopathology with GMS stain)",
            "属特異的PCR（Lagenidium vs Pythium鑑別） (Genus-specific PCR)",
            "ELISA血清抗体（Lagenidium特異的、入手可なら） (Lagenidium-specific ELISA)",
            "胸部・腹部CT（血管関与・播種評価） (Thoracic/abdominal CT)",
            "腹部超音波 (Abdominal ultrasound)",
            "全血球計算（好酸球増多） (CBC - eosinophilia)",
            "血液生化学検査 (Blood Chemistry Panel)",
            "局所リンパ節穿刺と細胞診 (Regional lymph node aspirate cytology)",
            "尿検査 (Urinalysis)",
        ],
        "urgency": "high",
        "onset_pattern": {"subacute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"young"},
    },
